al","duel":"banned","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"banned","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{U}{U}","name":"Time Warp","oracle_id":"dbd6a94b-62ff-4a10-9d52-bdd90b26e425","oracle_text":"Target player takes an extra turn after this one.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{R}{R}","name":"Warrior's Oath","oracle_id":"574044cf-2e2f-4b5c-b4d1-cf05ba814ab2","oracle_text":"Take an extra turn after this one. At the beginning of that turn's end step, you lose the game.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Chance for Glory’s first effect affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the game won’t gain indestructible.","oracle_id":"324af60d-142b-4b6c-afe9-6aa36267d5ee","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Creatures you control gain indestructible indefinitely. If you find a way to not lose the game during your next turn, they’ll continue to be indestructible for as long as they remain on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"324af60d-142b-4b6c-afe9-6aa36267d5ee","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you somehow skip the extra turn Chance for Glory gives you or skip that turn’s end step, the delayed triggered ability never triggers.","oracle_id":"324af60d-142b-4b6c-afe9-6aa36267d5ee","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you end up skipping the extra turn that is gained, you do not lose the game.","oracle_id":"8d0adc5c-3fdd-4e22-b783-5651f8e57b65","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple \"extra turn\" effects resolve in the same turn, take them in the reverse of the order that the effects resolved. In other words, the most recently created extra turn is taken first.","oracle_id":"8d0adc5c-3fdd-4e22-b783-5651f8e57b65","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple \"extra turn\" effects resolve in the same turn, take them in the reverse of the order that the effects resolved. In other words, the most recently created extra turn is taken first.","oracle_id":"dbd6a94b-62ff-4a10-9d52-bdd90b26e425","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You skip one turn as part of the effect.","oracle_id":"f79f84c9-2023-4348-863b-a3b4bc382904","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
